{"Removing locking of entire BuildIndex and only locking cache assignment can cause duplicate index builds when concurrent callers both see absent cache entry and both kick off builder functions": 0.9075618982315063, "NewResourceServer now calls s.Init(ctx) during construction, which blocks server creation if search initialization is slow and changes startup behavior": 0.677310049533844, "Initialization errors that were previously deferred until first request will now fail NewResourceServer, potentially breaking deployments that tolerated lazy init failures": 0.6146551370620728, "Changed tracer.Start usage from '_, span := tracer.Start(ctx, ...)' to 'ctx, span := tracer.Start(ctx, ...)' is correct but should scan codebase for other occurrences of the old pattern": 0.5199176669120789, "Moving initWatcher to after search.init changes lifecycle ordering - need to confirm watchers don't miss events while init is running": 0.6335197687149048, "Building all initial indices concurrently at startup could spike memory/IO causing higher load or out-of-memory situations": 0.3785001337528229, "Tests that relied on lazy init to avoid heavy work during setup will now do work during setup, causing potential test failures or longer-running tests": 0.10426978021860123, "Skipped postgres test with TODO needs to be addressed before merging or tracked in issue": 0.3399043381214142, "Health endpoint should reflect initialization progress - IsHealthy should return Unhealthy until init completes": 0.34861209988594055, "Need to verify no codepath tries to call search while Init hasn't been called after removing s.Init() calls from RPC handlers": 0.49689701199531555, "Caller of NewResourceServer should pass appropriate context with sensible deadline for startup": 0.482380747795105}